📂 File & Directory Management
ls → List files
ls -l → List with details (permissions, size, owner)
ls -a → Show hidden files (hidden files start with .)
pwd → Present working directory
/ → Root directory
mkdir folderName → Create directory
touch file.txt → Create file

❌ Delete Files & Folders
rm index.txt → Delete file
rm -r folderName/ → Delete folder + contents (⚠ recursive)
rmdir folderName/ → Delete empty folder

File Content Handling
cat file.txt → View file content
head file.txt → View top lines
tail file.txt → View last lines
tail -f file.txt → Monitor file changes (logs 🔥)
echo "Hello World" → Print text
echo "Hello World" > file.txt → Write text into file (creates file if not exists)

📁 Copy & Move
cp file.txt devops/ → Copy file
cp devops/file.txt cloud/ → Copy from one folder to another
cp -r cloud/ devops/ → Copy folder recursively
mv file.txt ../cloud/ → Move file
mv devops linux_for_devops → Rename folder

🔗 Links in Linux
 Soft link → breaks if original file is deleted
 Hard link → stays even if original file is deleted

📊 System Monitoring
df -h → Disk usage
free -h → Memory usage
vmstat → RAM & virtual memory stats
top → Running processes
